    "problemStatement": "You have a parameter KKK.\n\nConsider performing the following action on an array AAA of length NNN **exactly once**:\n\n\nChoose an integer MMM and then MMM intervals [L1,R1],[L2,R2],…,[LM,RM][L_1, R_1], [L_2, R_2], \\ldots, [L_M, R_M][L1​,R1​],[L2​,R2​],…,[LM​,RM​] such that:\n\n1≤Li≤Ri≤N1 \\le L_i \\le R_i \\le N1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N\nL1=1L_1 = 1L1​=1 and RM=NR_M = NRM​=N\nLi=Ri−1+1L_i = R_{i - 1} + 1Li​=Ri−1​+1 for all 2≤i≤M2 \\le i \\le M2≤i≤M\nRi−Li+1≤KR_i - L_i + 1 \\le KRi​−Li​+1≤K\n\n\nFor each i=1…Mi = 1 \\ldots Mi=1…M, sort A[Li,Ri]A[L_i, R_i]A[Li​,Ri​] (i.e. replace the subarray with the sorted version of it) where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] denotes the subarray [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​].\nLess formally, you divide the array into several subarrays, each of length at most KKK, and then sort each part and concatenate the pieces back together.\n\nDefine f(A)f(A)f(A) as the lexicographically minimum array possible at the end of the above process.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN. It is guaranteed that AAA is a permutation of integers in [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nSolve QQQ queries of the following type:\n\n\nYou are given 333 integers, LLL, RRR and XXX.\n\nLet B=A[L,R]B = A[L, R]B=A[L,R] and C=f(B)C = f(B)C=f(B). Find the XXX-th element in CCC, i.e. CXC_XCX​.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 333 integers - N,KN, KN,K and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next QQQ lines each contain 333 integers each - L,RL, RL,R and XXX representing a query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output QQQ integers on the same line - the answers to the queries in the same order.",
